WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.790
Coral reefs cover only about
1 per cent of the ocean.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.450
Yet they give habitat to at
least 25 per cent of marine life.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.450
Most lie in shallow seas, between about
35 degrees north and 35 degrees south.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.270
And tropical seas are nutrient-poor.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.090
Yet NOAA calls reefs among the most
productive and diverse marine environments

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.410
on Earth.

7
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.650
So where does the food come from?

8
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.290
Rivers?

9
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.030
Fish from the open ocean?

10
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.010
In this mission, you'll
build a reef, polyp by polyp,

11
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.630
from skeletons of calcium carbonate.

12
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.930
Then you'll follow the
food through a reef,

13
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.050
all the way to the sharks.

14
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: explain how coral reefs
teem with life in such nutrient-poor seas.
